.TH poi-tracker 1 2026-09-04 "sandogasa 0.22.0" "Sandogasa Manual"
.SH NAME
poi\-tracker \- Package\-of\-interest tracker for Fedora, EPEL, and CentOS SIGs
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBpoi\-tracker\fR [\fB\-i\fR|\fB\-\-inventory\fR] [\fB\-I\fR|\fB\-\-inventory\-dir\fR] [\fB\-w\fR|\fB\-\-workspace\fR] [\fB\-\-closure\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] [\fB\-V\fR|\fB\-\-version\fR] <\fIsubcommands\fR>
.SH DESCRIPTION
Package\-of\-interest tracker for Fedora, EPEL, and CentOS SIGs
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-i\fR, \fB\-\-inventory\fR \fI<INVENTORY>\fR
Path(s) to inventory TOML file(s)
.TP
\fB\-I\fR, \fB\-\-inventory\-dir\fR \fI<DIR>\fR
Directory to scan for *.toml inventory files
.TP
\fB\-w\fR, \fB\-\-workspace\fR \fI<PATH>\fR
Workspace file naming the inventories, graph and walk settings (default: ./kondo.toml when present). Supplies the flags the maintenance subcommands would otherwise need; the command line wins, \-\-no\-defaults ignores it
.TP
\fB\-\-closure\fR \fI<NAME>\fR
Which [[closure]] of the workspace a walk subcommand works on (default: the first)
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.TP
\fB\-V\fR, \fB\-\-version\fR
Print version
.SH COMMANDS
.SS poi-tracker act
\fBpoi\-tracker act\fR [\fB\-i\fR|\fB\-\-inventory\fR] <\fB\-\-user\fR> [\fB\-I\fR|\fB\-\-inventory\-dir\fR] [\fB\-\-pattern\fR] [\fB\-\-start\-from\fR] [\fB\-w\fR|\fB\-\-workspace\fR] [\fB\-\-closure\fR] [\fB\-\-end\-with\fR] [\fB\-\-personal\fR] [\fB\-\-branch\fR] [\fB\-\-api\-token\fR] [\fB\-\-refresh\-acls\fR] [\fB\-v\fR|\fB\-\-verbose\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] 
.PP
Enact the standing cull verdicts interactively: orphan, remove own ACL, or give each package away, adjusting the inventories as you go
.TP
\fB\-i\fR, \fB\-\-inventory\fR \fI<INVENTORY>\fR
Path(s) to inventory TOML file(s)
.TP
\fB\-\-user\fR \fI<USER>\fR
FAS username whose ACL actions these are
.TP
\fB\-I\fR, \fB\-\-inventory\-dir\fR \fI<DIR>\fR
Directory to scan for *.toml inventory files
.TP
\fB\-\-pattern\fR \fI<GLOB,...>\fR
Only process packages matching this glob (e.g. `rust\-*`; a bare name matches exactly). Comma\-separated or repeated; default: all packages
.TP
\fB\-\-start\-from\fR \fI<NAME>\fR
Resume from this package onwards (inclusive), in the inventory\*(Aqs iteration order
.TP
\fB\-w\fR, \fB\-\-workspace\fR \fI<PATH>\fR
Workspace file naming the inventories, graph and walk settings (default: ./kondo.toml when present). Supplies the flags the maintenance subcommands would otherwise need; the command line wins, \-\-no\-defaults ignores it
.TP
\fB\-\-closure\fR \fI<NAME>\fR
Which [[closure]] of the workspace a walk subcommand works on (default: the first)
.TP
\fB\-\-end\-with\fR \fI<NAME>\fR
Stop after this package (inclusive). Combine with `\-\-start\-from` to bound a sub\-range
.TP
\fB\-\-personal\fR \fI<PATH>\fR
Personal inventory to drop enacted packages from
.TP
\fB\-\-branch\fR \fI<BRANCH>\fR [default: auto]
Branch(es) for the reverse\-dependency probe before an orphan (CSV or repeated). The default `auto` derives them per package from its dist\-git branches: rawhide plus its own EPEL branches — an EPEL\-only package\*(Aqs dependents are invisible from rawhide
.TP
\fB\-\-api\-token\fR \fI<API_TOKEN>\fR
Dist\-git API token (or PAGURE_API_TOKEN, or run `poi\-tracker config`)
.RS
May also be specified with the \fBPAGURE_API_TOKEN\fR environment variable. 
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-refresh\-acls\fR
Ignore the day\-fresh ACL cache and look every level up again
.TP
\fB\-v\fR, \fB\-\-verbose\fR
Log each access lookup
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.SS poi-tracker add
\fBpoi\-tracker add\fR [\fB\-i\fR|\fB\-\-inventory\fR] [\fB\-\-poc\fR] [\fB\-I\fR|\fB\-\-inventory\-dir\fR] [\fB\-\-reason\fR] [\fB\-\-team\fR] [\fB\-w\fR|\fB\-\-workspace\fR] [\fB\-\-closure\fR] [\fB\-\-task\fR] [\fB\-\-rpm\fR] [\fB\-\-workload\fR] [\fB\-\-track\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fINAME\fR> 
.PP
Add a package to the inventory
.TP
\fB\-i\fR, \fB\-\-inventory\fR \fI<INVENTORY>\fR
Path(s) to inventory TOML file(s)
.TP
\fB\-\-poc\fR \fI<POC>\fR
Point of contact ("Name <email>")
.TP
\fB\-I\fR, \fB\-\-inventory\-dir\fR \fI<DIR>\fR
Directory to scan for *.toml inventory files
.TP
\fB\-\-reason\fR \fI<REASON>\fR
Reason for tracking
.TP
\fB\-\-team\fR \fI<TEAM>\fR
Team responsible
.TP
\fB\-w\fR, \fB\-\-workspace\fR \fI<PATH>\fR
Workspace file naming the inventories, graph and walk settings (default: ./kondo.toml when present). Supplies the flags the maintenance subcommands would otherwise need; the command line wins, \-\-no\-defaults ignores it
.TP
\fB\-\-closure\fR \fI<NAME>\fR
Which [[closure]] of the workspace a walk subcommand works on (default: the first)
.TP
\fB\-\-task\fR \fI<TASK>\fR
Internal task/ticket reference
.TP
\fB\-\-rpm\fR \fI<RPM>\fR
Binary RPM subpackage(s) to track (comma\-separated or repeated)
.TP
\fB\-\-workload\fR \fI<WORKLOAD>\fR
Workload tag(s) (comma\-separated or repeated)
.TP
\fB\-\-track\fR \fI<TRACK>\fR
Track branch for hs\-relmon (e.g. upstream, fedora\-rawhide)
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.TP
<\fINAME\fR>
Source RPM name
.SS poi-tracker adopt
\fBpoi\-tracker adopt\fR [\fB\-i\fR|\fB\-\-inventory\fR] [\fB\-\-pattern\fR] [\fB\-I\fR|\fB\-\-inventory\-dir\fR] [\fB\-\-start\-from\fR] [\fB\-\-end\-with\fR] [\fB\-w\fR|\fB\-\-workspace\fR] [\fB\-\-api\-token\fR] [\fB\-\-closure\fR] [\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR] [\fB\-y\fR|\fB\-\-yes\fR] [\fB\-v\fR|\fB\-\-verbose\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] 
.PP
Adopt orphaned inventory packages on dist\-git
.TP
\fB\-i\fR, \fB\-\-inventory\fR \fI<INVENTORY>\fR
Path(s) to inventory TOML file(s)
.TP
\fB\-\-pattern\fR \fI<GLOB,...>\fR
Only process packages matching this glob (e.g. `rust\-*`; a bare name matches exactly). Comma\-separated or repeated; default: all packages
.TP
\fB\-I\fR, \fB\-\-inventory\-dir\fR \fI<DIR>\fR
Directory to scan for *.toml inventory files
.TP
\fB\-\-start\-from\fR \fI<NAME>\fR
Resume from this package onwards (inclusive), in the inventory\*(Aqs iteration order
.TP
\fB\-\-end\-with\fR \fI<NAME>\fR
Stop after this package (inclusive). Combine with `\-\-start\-from` to bound a sub\-range
.TP
\fB\-w\fR, \fB\-\-workspace\fR \fI<PATH>\fR
Workspace file naming the inventories, graph and walk settings (default: ./kondo.toml when present). Supplies the flags the maintenance subcommands would otherwise need; the command line wins, \-\-no\-defaults ignores it
.TP
\fB\-\-api\-token\fR \fI<API_TOKEN>\fR
Dist\-git API token with the `modify_project` ACL (or set PAGURE_API_TOKEN, or run `poi\-tracker config`)
.RS
May also be specified with the \fBPAGURE_API_TOKEN\fR environment variable. 
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-closure\fR \fI<NAME>\fR
Which [[closure]] of the workspace a walk subcommand works on (default: the first)
.TP
\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR
Preview orphaned packages without adopting them
.TP
\fB\-y\fR, \fB\-\-yes\fR
Adopt every orphaned match without per\-package prompts
.TP
\fB\-v\fR, \fB\-\-verbose\fR
Print progress to stderr
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.SS poi-tracker announce
\fBpoi\-tracker announce\fR [\fB\-i\fR|\fB\-\-inventory\fR] <\fB\-\-user\fR> [\fB\-I\fR|\fB\-\-inventory\-dir\fR] [\fB\-\-refresh\-acls\fR] [\fB\-v\fR|\fB\-\-verbose\fR] [\fB\-w\fR|\fB\-\-workspace\fR] [\fB\-\-closure\fR] [\fB\-\-json\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] 
.PP
Render the standing cull verdicts as the grouped, announcement\-ready report with runnable ACL commands
.TP
\fB\-i\fR, \fB\-\-inventory\fR \fI<INVENTORY>\fR
Path(s) to inventory TOML file(s)
.TP
\fB\-\-user\fR \fI<USER>\fR
FAS username whose access level routes each action
.TP
\fB\-I\fR, \fB\-\-inventory\-dir\fR \fI<DIR>\fR
Directory to scan for *.toml inventory files
.TP
\fB\-\-refresh\-acls\fR
Ignore the day\-fresh ACL cache and look every level up again
.TP
\fB\-v\fR, \fB\-\-verbose\fR
Log each access lookup
.TP
\fB\-w\fR, \fB\-\-workspace\fR \fI<PATH>\fR
Workspace file naming the inventories, graph and walk settings (default: ./kondo.toml when present). Supplies the flags the maintenance subcommands would otherwise need; the command line wins, \-\-no\-defaults ignores it
.TP
\fB\-\-closure\fR \fI<NAME>\fR
Which [[closure]] of the workspace a walk subcommand works on (default: the first)
.TP
\fB\-\-json\fR
Output machine\-readable JSON
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.SS poi-tracker config
\fBpoi\-tracker config\fR [\fB\-i\fR|\fB\-\-inventory\fR] [\fB\-I\fR|\fB\-\-inventory\-dir\fR] [\fB\-w\fR|\fB\-\-workspace\fR] [\fB\-\-closure\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] 
.PP
Configure poi\-tracker (Bugzilla API key, etc.)
.TP
\fB\-i\fR, \fB\-\-inventory\fR \fI<INVENTORY>\fR
Path(s) to inventory TOML file(s)
.TP
\fB\-I\fR, \fB\-\-inventory\-dir\fR \fI<DIR>\fR
Directory to scan for *.toml inventory files
.TP
\fB\-w\fR, \fB\-\-workspace\fR \fI<PATH>\fR
Workspace file naming the inventories, graph and walk settings (default: ./kondo.toml when present). Supplies the flags the maintenance subcommands would otherwise need; the command line wins, \-\-no\-defaults ignores it
.TP
\fB\-\-closure\fR \fI<NAME>\fR
Which [[closure]] of the workspace a walk subcommand works on (default: the first)
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.SS poi-tracker dependents
\fBpoi\-tracker dependents\fR <\fB\-\-graph\fR> [\fB\-i\fR|\fB\-\-inventory\fR] [\fB\-I\fR|\fB\-\-inventory\-dir\fR] [\fB\-\-json\fR] [\fB\-w\fR|\fB\-\-workspace\fR] [\fB\-\-closure\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] 
.PP
Classify inventory packages by who depends on them, over a saved dependency graph: leaves, packages other keeps carry, externally needed ones
.TP
\fB\-\-graph\fR \fI<PATH>\fR
Dependency graph JSON from a `deps \-\-graph` run
.TP
\fB\-i\fR, \fB\-\-inventory\fR \fI<INVENTORY>\fR
Path(s) to inventory TOML file(s)
.TP
\fB\-I\fR, \fB\-\-inventory\-dir\fR \fI<DIR>\fR
Directory to scan for *.toml inventory files
.TP
\fB\-\-json\fR
Output machine\-readable JSON
.TP
\fB\-w\fR, \fB\-\-workspace\fR \fI<PATH>\fR
Workspace file naming the inventories, graph and walk settings (default: ./kondo.toml when present). Supplies the flags the maintenance subcommands would otherwise need; the command line wins, \-\-no\-defaults ignores it
.TP
\fB\-\-closure\fR \fI<NAME>\fR
Which [[closure]] of the workspace a walk subcommand works on (default: the first)
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.SS poi-tracker deps
\fBpoi\-tracker deps\fR [\fB\-i\fR|\fB\-\-inventory\fR] [\fB\-\-pattern\fR] [\fB\-I\fR|\fB\-\-inventory\-dir\fR] [\fB\-\-start\-from\fR] [\fB\-\-end\-with\fR] [\fB\-w\fR|\fB\-\-workspace\fR] <\fB\-b\fR|\fB\-\-branch\fR> [\fB\-\-closure\fR] [\fB\-r\fR|\fB\-\-repo\fR] [\fB\-\-from\fR] [\fB\-\-base\-repo\fR] [\fB\-\-runtime\-only\fR] [\fB\-\-graph\fR] [\fB\-\-fixpoint\fR] [\fB\-o\fR|\fB\-\-output\fR] [\fB\-\-name\fR] [\fB\-\-json\fR] [\fB\-v\fR|\fB\-\-verbose\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] 
.PP
Inventory the dependencies pulled from other repos (e.g. EPEL)
.TP
\fB\-i\fR, \fB\-\-inventory\fR \fI<INVENTORY>\fR
Path(s) to inventory TOML file(s)
.TP
\fB\-\-pattern\fR \fI<GLOB,...>\fR
Only process packages matching this glob (e.g. `rust\-*`; a bare name matches exactly). Comma\-separated or repeated; default: all packages
.TP
\fB\-I\fR, \fB\-\-inventory\-dir\fR \fI<DIR>\fR
Directory to scan for *.toml inventory files
.TP
\fB\-\-start\-from\fR \fI<NAME>\fR
Resume from this package onwards (inclusive), in the inventory\*(Aqs iteration order
.TP
\fB\-\-end\-with\fR \fI<NAME>\fR
Stop after this package (inclusive). Combine with `\-\-start\-from` to bound a sub\-range
.TP
\fB\-w\fR, \fB\-\-workspace\fR \fI<PATH>\fR
Workspace file naming the inventories, graph and walk settings (default: ./kondo.toml when present). Supplies the flags the maintenance subcommands would otherwise need; the command line wins, \-\-no\-defaults ignores it
.TP
\fB\-b\fR, \fB\-\-branch\fR \fI<BRANCH>\fR
fedrq branch (e.g. hs.el9, epel9)
.TP
\fB\-\-closure\fR \fI<NAME>\fR
Which [[closure]] of the workspace a walk subcommand works on (default: the first)
.TP
\fB\-r\fR, \fB\-\-repo\fR \fI<REPO>\fR
fedrq repo class (e.g. stack)
.TP
\fB\-\-from\fR \fI<FROM>\fR [default: epel]
Collect providers from these repo ids (CSV or repeated).

Exact match. The default suits an EPEL walk; for a Fedora walk pass the branch\*(Aqs own repo id, e.g. `\-\-from rawhide`.
.TP
\fB\-\-base\-repo\fR \fI<BASE_REPO>\fR [default: fedrq\-centos\-stream\-]
Base\-distro repo id prefix(es); their providers end the walk.

The default treats CentOS Stream as the given beneath an EPEL stack. A Fedora walk has no base distro — the default then never matches, and everything resolves within \-\-from\*(Aqs repos, which is what you want.
.TP
\fB\-\-runtime\-only\fR
Walk runtime dependencies only, without seeding the roots\*(Aq BuildRequires
.TP
\fB\-\-graph\fR \fI<PATH>\fR
Where to write the walk\*(Aqs full dependency graph (every requirer/provider edge, not just first attributions) as JSON. Default: beside \-o, as <output>\-graph.json
.TP
\fB\-\-fixpoint\fR \fI<PATH>\fR
Iterate to a fixpoint: collected packages found in this inventory (yours) become roots whose BuildRequires seed further rounds
.TP
\fB\-o\fR, \fB\-\-output\fR \fI<OUTPUT>\fR
Write the collected dependencies as an inventory TOML file
.TP
\fB\-\-name\fR \fI<NAME>\fR
Inventory name for \-\-output (default: "<input name>\-deps\-<branch>")
.TP
\fB\-\-json\fR
Output as JSON instead of human\-readable
.TP
\fB\-v\fR, \fB\-\-verbose\fR
Print progress to stderr
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
.SS poi-tracker derive
\fBpoi\-tracker derive\fR <\fB\-\-graph\fR> [\fB\-i\fR|\fB\-\-inventory\fR] [\fB\-I\fR|\fB\-\-inventory\-dir\fR] <\fB\-\-owned\fR> <\fB\-o\fR|\fB\-\-output\fR> [\fB\-w\fR|\fB\-\-workspace\fR] [\fB\-\-apply\fR] [\fB\-\-closure\fR] [\fB\-\-json\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] 
.PP
Recompute a derived dependency inventory offline from a saved graph: owned packages the keeps reach
.TP
\fB\-\-graph\fR \fI<PATH>\fR
Dependency graph JSON from a `deps \-\-graph` run
.TP
\fB\-i\fR, \fB\-\-inventory\fR \fI<INVENTORY>\fR
Path(s) to inventory TOML file(s)
.TP
\fB\-I\fR, \fB\-\-inventory\-dir\fR \fI<DIR>\fR
Directory to scan for *.toml inventory files
.TP
\fB\-\-owned\fR \fI<PATH>\fR
Inventory of the packages you own (e.g. a sync\-distgit output); only owned packages enter the derived inventory
.TP
\fB\-o\fR, \fB\-\-output\fR \fI<PATH>\fR
The derived inventory to recompute
.TP
\fB\-w\fR, \fB\-\-workspace\fR \fI<PATH>\fR
Workspace file naming the inventories, graph and walk settings (default: ./kondo.toml when present). Supplies the flags the maintenance subcommands would otherwise need; the command line wins, \-\-no\-defaults ignores it
.TP
\fB\-\-apply\fR
Replace the output file\*(Aqs packages; without it, report only
.TP
\fB\-\-closure\fR \fI<NAME>\fR
Which [[closure]] of the workspace a walk subcommand works on (default: the first)
.TP
\fB\-\-json\fR
Output machine\-readable JSON
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.SS poi-tracker export
\fBpoi\-tracker export\fR [\fB\-i\fR|\fB\-\-inventory\fR] [\fB\-I\fR|\fB\-\-inventory\-dir\fR] [\fB\-w\fR|\fB\-\-workspace\fR] [\fB\-\-closure\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fIsubcommands\fR>
.PP
Export inventory to another format
.TP
\fB\-i\fR, \fB\-\-inventory\fR \fI<INVENTORY>\fR
Path(s) to inventory TOML file(s)
.TP
\fB\-I\fR, \fB\-\-inventory\-dir\fR \fI<DIR>\fR
Directory to scan for *.toml inventory files
.TP
\fB\-w\fR, \fB\-\-workspace\fR \fI<PATH>\fR
Workspace file naming the inventories, graph and walk settings (default: ./kondo.toml when present). Supplies the flags the maintenance subcommands would otherwise need; the command line wins, \-\-no\-defaults ignores it
.TP
\fB\-\-closure\fR \fI<NAME>\fR
Which [[closure]] of the workspace a walk subcommand works on (default: the first)
