\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.SS poi-tracker keep
\fBpoi\-tracker keep\fR [\fB\-i\fR|\fB\-\-inventory\fR] [\fB\-\-into\fR] <\fB\-\-graph\fR> [\fB\-I\fR|\fB\-\-inventory\-dir\fR] <\fB\-\-owned\fR> [\fB\-w\fR|\fB\-\-workspace\fR] [\fB\-\-closure\fR] [\fB\-\-deps\fR] <\fB\-b\fR|\fB\-\-branch\fR> [\fB\-r\fR|\fB\-\-repo\fR] [\fB\-\-from\fR] [\fB\-\-base\-repo\fR] [\fB\-\-runtime\-only\fR] [\fB\-\-json\fR] [\fB\-v\fR|\fB\-\-verbose\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fIPACKAGE\fR> 
.PP
Start keeping packages: walk them against the saved graph (fedrq only for what it lacks), merge, recompute the derived inventory
.TP
\fB\-i\fR, \fB\-\-inventory\fR \fI<INVENTORY>\fR
Path(s) to inventory TOML file(s)
.TP
\fB\-\-into\fR \fI<PATH>\fR
Keep inventory to add them to (default: the first \-i)
.TP
\fB\-\-graph\fR \fI<PATH>\fR
Saved dependency graph to extend (from `deps`); the walk resolves offline whatever it already knows
.TP
\fB\-I\fR, \fB\-\-inventory\-dir\fR \fI<DIR>\fR
Directory to scan for *.toml inventory files
.TP
\fB\-\-owned\fR \fI<PATH>\fR
Inventory of the packages you own — newly reached owned packages become fixpoint roots and derived entries
.TP
\fB\-w\fR, \fB\-\-workspace\fR \fI<PATH>\fR
Workspace file naming the inventories, graph and walk settings (default: ./kondo.toml when present). Supplies the flags the maintenance subcommands would otherwise need; the command line wins, \-\-no\-defaults ignores it
.TP
\fB\-\-closure\fR \fI<NAME>\fR
Which [[closure]] of the workspace a walk subcommand works on (default: the first)
.TP
\fB\-\-deps\fR \fI<PATH>\fR
Derived inventory to recompute afterwards (optional)
.TP
\fB\-b\fR, \fB\-\-branch\fR \fI<BRANCH>\fR
fedrq branch (e.g. hs.el9, epel9)
.TP
\fB\-r\fR, \fB\-\-repo\fR \fI<REPO>\fR
fedrq repo class (e.g. stack)
.TP
\fB\-\-from\fR \fI<FROM>\fR [default: epel]
Collect providers from these repo ids (CSV or repeated).

Exact match. The default suits an EPEL walk; for a Fedora walk pass the branch\*(Aqs own repo id, e.g. `\-\-from rawhide`.
.TP
\fB\-\-base\-repo\fR \fI<BASE_REPO>\fR [default: fedrq\-centos\-stream\-]
Base\-distro repo id prefix(es); their providers end the walk.

The default treats CentOS Stream as the given beneath an EPEL stack. A Fedora walk has no base distro — the default then never matches, and everything resolves within \-\-from\*(Aqs repos, which is what you want.
.TP
\fB\-\-runtime\-only\fR
Walk runtime dependencies only, without seeding the roots\*(Aq BuildRequires
.TP
\fB\-\-json\fR
Output as JSON instead of human\-readable
.TP
\fB\-v\fR, \fB\-\-verbose\fR
Print progress to stderr
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
.TP
<\fIPACKAGE\fR>
Packages to start keeping
.SS poi-tracker kondo
\fBpoi\-tracker kondo\fR [\fB\-i\fR|\fB\-\-inventory\fR] [\fB\-\-pattern\fR] [\fB\-I\fR|\fB\-\-inventory\-dir\fR] [\fB\-\-start\-from\fR] [\fB\-\-end\-with\fR] [\fB\-w\fR|\fB\-\-workspace\fR] [\fB\-\-closure\fR] <\fB\-\-essential\fR> <\fB\-\-user\fR> [\fB\-\-explain\-into\fR] [\fB\-y\fR|\fB\-\-yes\fR] [\fB\-\-refresh\-acls\fR] [\fB\-\-reason\fR] [\fB\-o\fR|\fB\-\-output\fR] [\fB\-\-json\fR] [\fB\-v\fR|\fB\-\-verbose\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] 
.PP
Triage packages no essential inventory needs: keep as a cull candidate, file into an inventory, or drop
.TP
\fB\-i\fR, \fB\-\-inventory\fR \fI<INVENTORY>\fR
Path(s) to inventory TOML file(s)
.TP
\fB\-\-pattern\fR \fI<GLOB,...>\fR
Only process packages matching this glob (e.g. `rust\-*`; a bare name matches exactly). Comma\-separated or repeated; default: all packages
.TP
\fB\-I\fR, \fB\-\-inventory\-dir\fR \fI<DIR>\fR
Directory to scan for *.toml inventory files
.TP
\fB\-\-start\-from\fR \fI<NAME>\fR
Resume from this package onwards (inclusive), in the inventory\*(Aqs iteration order
.TP
\fB\-\-end\-with\fR \fI<NAME>\fR
Stop after this package (inclusive). Combine with `\-\-start\-from` to bound a sub\-range
.TP
\fB\-w\fR, \fB\-\-workspace\fR \fI<PATH>\fR
Workspace file naming the inventories, graph and walk settings (default: ./kondo.toml when present). Supplies the flags the maintenance subcommands would otherwise need; the command line wins, \-\-no\-defaults ignores it
.TP
\fB\-\-closure\fR \fI<NAME>\fR
Which [[closure]] of the workspace a walk subcommand works on (default: the first)
.TP
\fB\-\-essential\fR \fI<ESSENTIAL>\fR
Essential inventory file(s): packages found in any of these are never cull candidates (repeat the flag per file)
.TP
\fB\-\-user\fR \fI<USER>\fR
dist\-git username whose access level routes each action
.TP
\fB\-\-explain\-into\fR \fI<PATH>\fR
Default inventory for \*(Aqexplain\*(Aq: Enter at the explanation prompt files the package here
.TP
\fB\-y\fR, \fB\-\-yes\fR
Keep every candidate without prompting
.TP
\fB\-\-refresh\-acls\fR
Ignore the day\-fresh ACL cache and look every level up again
.TP
\fB\-\-reason\fR \fI<REASON>\fR
Reason recorded in the \-o cull file for packages culled this run (the access level is always appended). A note typed at the prompt as `k <note>` overrides it per package
.TP
\fB\-o\fR, \fB\-\-output\fR \fI<OUTPUT>\fR
Merge the culled set into this inventory TOML file (accumulates across passes)
.TP
\fB\-\-json\fR
Output as JSON instead of human\-readable
.TP
\fB\-v\fR, \fB\-\-verbose\fR
Print progress to stderr
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.SS poi-tracker prune-retired
\fBpoi\-tracker prune\-retired\fR [\fB\-\-branch\fR] [\fB\-i\fR|\fB\-\-inventory\fR] [\fB\-I\fR|\fB\-\-inventory\-dir\fR] [\fB\-\-pattern\fR] [\fB\-\-start\-from\fR] [\fB\-w\fR|\fB\-\-workspace\fR] [\fB\-\-closure\fR] [\fB\-\-end\-with\fR] [\fB\-j\fR|\fB\-\-jobs\fR] [\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR] [\fB\-\-remove\fR] [\fB\-y\fR|\fB\-\-yes\fR] [\fB\-v\fR|\fB\-\-verbose\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] 
